# settled-crowd: a body whose way is closed by a settled crowd of its own side, arrived for another destination.
# Order A (24 bodies) settles in the middle of a corridor 8 cells wide and fills it from wall to wall. At tick 1,500
# order B (6 bodies) is sent through the corridor to a point beyond it; the corridor is its only way.
# The settled bodies cannot open a lane (a settled body steps at most one cell from its goal), the local detour is
# smaller than the crowd, and the settle rule ignores a settled crowd of another destination: B stood in front of
# A for good, orders kept. Its orders now end beside the crowd (the stand-down: the Legion counterpart of Retail's
# growing goal circle), and the units are free for the next order.
# Read at start offset 0 only (legion_settledcrowd). A negative start offset moves order B's spawn to within two
# cells of the map's edge, where three of its six bodies cannot move in either mode (Retail leaves them standing
# there as well): they never reach the crowd, hold their orders to the long stand-down, 4,808 ticks after the
# order, and this file ends before that.
# Keys: open_still900 (0; 6 before), g.B.complete_n (6; 0 before), work.stand_downs.total.
scn 1
name settled-crowd
ticks 4500
seed 7
players 1
weapons off
map flat 128 40
wall 34 0 60 16
wall 34 24 60 16
type m mover 2 2500 10 1.79999
group A 0 m 24 rect 4 8 24 32 pitch=3
group B 0 m 6 rect 4 4 12 8 pitch=3
at 2 move A 64 20
at 1500 move B 112 20
